# Departments that use neither an enabled `retry` table nor `wrap_pipeline_failure`.
# Omitted `retry` inherits the engine's reliable host defaults, exactly like `retry = {}`;
# `retry = false` is the explicit opt-out. This inventory tracks package-owned explicitness,
# not deliveries dropped because retry was omitted.
#
# Format: <package>.<department>|issue=#N|why=<one-line reason>
#
# SHRINK-ONLY. New entries fail CI. Remove an entry by giving the department a `retry` policy
# or `wrap_pipeline_failure` -- never by widening the structural exemptions in
# scripts/check_repo_dept_failure_surface.py.
#
# `dead_letter` and `test_*` departments are structurally exempt by role and are not listed.
github-devloop.liveness_scan|issue=#2996|why=liveness sweep drives every stuck-state redrive; its package-owned failure surface remains implicit. Highest priority to remove.
